# NOT overridable per-path: a `/favicon.svg` block with its own Cache-Control was tried
# 2026-07-28 and Pages CONCATENATED the two values rather than letting the more specific
# path win — the icon shipped with the self-contradicting
# `no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, public, max-age=604800`. The /* no-store is correct
# for the consoles (they must never serve stale), and re-validating a 1.2 KB icon is not
# worth a malformed header, so the brandmark deliberately inherits it.

# connect-src MUST list 'self'. Specifying connect-src at all overrides default-src for
# fetch/XHR, so without 'self' the page cannot fetch its OWN files -- including the
# metrics.json fallback that exists precisely for when the hosted row is unreachable. Shipped
# without it on 2026-08-19 and the fallback was blocked by this policy on every load: the page
# sat on "connecting..." and rendered dashes, looking identical to the outage it was added to
# survive. The Supabase origin is kept so a restored project needs no header change.
